error[type]: ? operator can only be used inside a function that returns Result or Option
 --> try__a_question_that_ends_a_closure_is_the_one_error_around_it.silt:10:26
    |
 10 |   Ok(list.map(xs) { s -> int.parse(s)? + 1 })
    |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ ? operator can only be used inside a function that returns Result or Option
  = note: the ?-ed expression is Result(Int, int.IntError), but the closure it is in returns Int
  = help: a `?` in a closure ends the closure, not the function; over a list, `list.traverse(xs) { x -> ... }?` calls the closure on every element, then gives the first `Err`; to stop at the first `Err`, use `list.fold_until` or a `loop`

